---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const heroImg = SITE.ogImage;
const secondImg = SITE.secondaryImage;
const mailto = `mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=area51.monster%20Acquisition%20Inquiry&body=I'm%20interested%20in%20acquiring%20area51.monster%20and/or%20the%20associated%20story%20concept.`;
---
<BaseLayout preloadImage={heroImg}>
  <div aria-hidden="true" style="pointer-events:none;position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:99;background:repeating-linear-gradient(0deg,rgba(0,0,0,0.12) 0px,rgba(0,0,0,0.12) 1px,transparent 1px,transparent 2px);"></div>
  <Nav active="/" />

  <main id="main">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="min-height:100vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;align-items:center;text-align:center;padding:5rem 2rem 3rem;position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
      <div
        aria-hidden="true"
        style={`position:absolute;inset:0;background:url('${heroImg}') center/cover no-repeat,#000;opacity:0.38;`}
      ></div>

      <div style="position:relative;z-index:1;max-width:860px;">
        <p style="letter-spacing:0.4em;font-size:0.75rem;color:#00ff41;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:1.2rem;">CLASSIFIED // NV-51 // EYES ONLY</p>

        <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.4rem,7vw,5.5rem);font-weight:900;line-height:1.05;color:#fff;letter-spacing:-0.02em;text-transform:uppercase;">
          AREA<span style="color:#00ff41;">51</span>.MONSTER
        </h1>

        <p style="margin:1.5rem auto 0;font-size:clamp(1rem,2.5vw,1.35rem);max-width:640px;line-height:1.7;color:#b0b0b0;">
          Deep beneath the Nevada desert, miles of excavated earth have carved out the most classified real estate on the planet — alien spacecraft hangars, subterranean tunnels stretching toward the Pacific coast, and a story the world has never been allowed to read.
        </p>

        <p style="margin:1.2rem auto 0;font-size:clamp(0.9rem,2vw,1.1rem);max-width:580px;line-height:1.7;color:#6a6a6a;font-style:italic;">
          So much earth has been removed from this site that what remains below defies conventional explanation. Spaceship storage. Tunnel networks. Ocean access.
        </p>

        <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
          <a href={mailto} class="btn">ACQUIRE THIS DOMAIN</a>
          <p class="btn-note">{SITE.email} // CLEARED INQUIRIES ONLY</p>
        </div>

        <p style="margin-top:2.2rem;font-size:0.68rem;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4a4a4a;">
          <a href="/acquisition/" style="color:#4a4a4a;">DOMAIN FOR SALE</a> //
          <a href="/film-concept/" style="color:#4a4a4a;">SCRIPT &amp; SERIES IP</a> //
          <a href="/faq/" style="color:#4a4a4a;">ACQUISITION FAQ</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Dossier index — internal link hub -->
    <section class="container" aria-labelledby="dossiers-heading">
      <h2 id="dossiers-heading" class="h2">Decrypted Dossiers</h2>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Four files cleared for public release. Each document opens a different vector of the same underground.</p>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>
          <a href="/story/">
            <span class="file-title">01 // The Excavation Story</span>
            <span class="file-meta">Geological anomaly · tunnel network · Pacific terminal</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/film-concept/">
            <span class="file-title">02 // Film &amp; Series Concept</span>
            <span class="file-meta">Logline · synopsis · development package</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/acquisition/">
            <span class="file-title">03 // Domain &amp; IP Acquisition</span>
            <span class="file-meta">area51.monster for sale · licensing · escrow</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/faq/">
            <span class="file-title">04 // Acquisition FAQ</span>
            <span class="file-meta">Process · inclusions · contact protocol</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Story teaser -->
    <section class="container" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
      <h2 id="story-heading" class="h2">The Excavation Story</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The sheer volume of earth displaced at and around the Area 51 complex in the Nevada desert is a geological anomaly that has never been fully accounted for. Official narratives describe test aircraft and radar experimentation. They do not account for cubic miles of removed desert floor.
        </p>
        <p>
          What if the excavations served a different purpose entirely? An underground storage complex of unprecedented scale — designed not for human aircraft, but for vehicles that did not originate on this planet. Hangars carved from bedrock. Climate-controlled vaults. A network of pressurized tunnels following the geography westward, terminating somewhere along the Pacific.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2.5rem 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
        <img
          src={secondImg}
          alt="Subterranean Nevada desert excavation site with classified underground infrastructure"
          width="800"
          height="450"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;opacity:0.82;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;"
        />
        <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;font-size:0.65rem;color:#2a2a2a;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;">CLASSIFIED IMAGERY // NV-51 SECTOR</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The tunnel-to-ocean hypothesis is not new. What is new is the narrative architecture built around it — a <a href="/film-concept/">script concept</a>, a world, a mythology ready for film or series development.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/story/">Read the full excavation file →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Acquisition teaser -->
    <section class="container" aria-labelledby="acq-heading">
      <h2 id="acq-heading" class="h2">For Acquisition</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>area51.monster</strong> is available for domain acquisition, story concept licensing, movie script sale, or film/series development partnership. The domain name, the narrative IP, and the conceptual framework are offered as a single package or individually.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>⬡ &nbsp;Domain acquisition — <strong>area51.monster</strong></li>
          <li>⬡ &nbsp;Movie script — Nevada underground / tunnel system concept</li>
          <li>⬡ &nbsp;Series development deal — classified mythology universe</li>
          <li>⬡ &nbsp;IP licensing — alien storage / desert mythology</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/acquisition/">Full acquisition details &amp; process →</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-band">
        <p>SIGNAL ACQUISITION PROTOCOL</p>
        <a href={mailto} class="btn">OPEN ACQUISITION CHANNEL</a>
        <p class="btn-note" style="margin-top:0.9rem;">{SITE.email}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ preview for rich results + internal link -->
    <section class="container" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="h2">Frequently Asked</h2>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is area51.monster for sale?</h3>
        <p>Yes. The domain, the screenplay concept, and the wider mythology IP are available — separately or as one package. See the <a href="/acquisition/">acquisition page</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Can the story be optioned for film or TV?</h3>
        <p>Yes. The concept is written for development — logline, synopsis, and series potential are outlined in the <a href="/film-concept/">film concept file</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;"><a href="/faq/">All acquisition questions →</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
